WEBVTT

00:00:00.053 --> 00:00:03.750
A new concept delegated authority You already know what

00:00:03.776 --> 00:00:06.039
it means to be able to edit a calendar

00:00:06.934 --> 00:00:10.039
Delegated authority is the specific permission to make a

00:00:10.092 --> 00:00:13.447
decision or act within an agreed scope and conditions

00:00:14.368 --> 00:00:16.842
Being able to use the system is a different

00:00:16.961 --> 00:00:21.211
fact The two situations below help you decide whether

00:00:21.276 --> 00:00:25.118
Daniel is permitted to act In the first all

00:00:25.184 --> 00:00:29.224
conditions of the supplied delegation are met In the

00:00:29.316 --> 00:00:33.539
second system access exists but decision authority does not

00:00:34.487 --> 00:00:37.803
Compare the permission and conditions not how easy the

00:00:37.908 --> 00:00:41.513
action would be to carry out Within the supplied

00:00:41.566 --> 00:00:45.987
delegation Daniel moves a routine internal administrative catch-up inside

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:51.447
an agreed free period No protected commitment external undertaking

00:00:51.855 --> 00:00:55.657
cost or specialist dependency is affected and the actual

00:00:55.697 --> 00:01:00.289
delegation permits it Not established by access Daniel can

00:01:00.329 --> 00:01:04.118
edit a supplier record That does not authorise him

00:01:04.170 --> 00:01:08.605
to approve a bank-detail change The appointed finance owner

00:01:08.618 --> 00:01:13.211
must handle the supplied verification / decision route The

00:01:13.237 --> 00:01:17.947
next classification activity lets you apply the distinction The

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:21.079
changed case in Activity 16 checks whether you can

00:01:21.197 --> 00:01:23.250
use it outside the diary example
